{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxwHnNagVaEPzargJGwe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done, and reading the rule back shows it is enabled.\n\n1. **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' points at the `kibana_sample_data_flights` index. Its time field is `timestamp`. The fields used below are `Carrier` (string) and `Cancelled` (boolean).\n2. **Dashboard:** I created 'S4-1c895f57 Flights' (id `s4-1c895f57-flights-66d7177630b7`) with exactly two panels:\n   - a line chart of the flight count over `timestamp`\n   - a bar chart of the flight count for the top 10 values of `Carrier`\n3. **Alert rule:** I created 'S4-1c895f57 Cancelled flights' (id `ab07f2d9-e3ea-4832-aae7-94d8ceb598db`). It is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It counts flights where `Cancelled` is true in the last 5 minutes and fires when there are more than 10. I created it already enabled, so no separate enable step was needed.\n4. **Edit and check:** I gave the carrier panel (panel index 1) the title 'Flights by carrier'. I had already used that title when creating the dashboard, so the edit kept the same name. Reading the rule back showed `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":607,"cache_read_input_tokens":20344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":607},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"ca2aefea-bc9b-4873-83bd-8a92372df7dd","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:00:07.232Z","request_id":"req_011CfxwHmpLHQrkt24uvt4cr"}
